From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: tomaszstaniak <68373859+tomaszstaniak@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 00:49:51 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] AROS: add native CPU frontend and independent launch
 rendering policy

Make native GPU dependencies optional and retain the upstream CPU image pipeline. Keep the desktop GPU feature explicit while the AROS build excludes wgpu. Enforce a process CPU policy that preferences and legacy GPU environment variables cannot undo.

Add a small LightcraftApp/Services adapter using egui-aros, persistent settings/catalog, ASL and upstream shutdown. Isolate Workbench/ToolTypes, DOS locks and path conversion in a safe platform boundary; copy system-owned icon data before freeing it. Select -nix explicitly and preserve the main task directory before workers. Use one launch parser for CLI and ToolTypes with independent CPU/AUTO/GPU requests.

